  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have RNA-only (0.485) and multimodal+ResNet50+concat (0.527), but we lack the image-only baseline. Without it, the 4.2-point multimodal gain cannot be decomposed: we don't know whether the image encoder alone carries most of the signal, whether the gain is truly synergistic, or whether the concat fusion mechanism is doing the heavy lifting. config_010 (image-only, single profile, ResNet50) is a clean single-axis ablation of config_016 (removing RNA) and a natural complement to config_001. This completes the three-way ablation triangle (RNA-only / image-only / multimodal), which is the most fundamental uncertainty in the current evidence. Resolving it directly informs whether to invest remaining budget in better image encoders (ViT-L), alternative fusion (weighted), or multiprofile settings—making it the highest-information use of the next experiment."
}

